Step 8: Sources of Error and Suggestions for Improvement
      :root {
        color-scheme: light;
        font-family: "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif;
      }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        background: #f4efe8;
        color: #2c241f;
      }
      main {
        max-width: 48rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 2rem 1.25rem 2.5rem;
      }
      .panel {
        background: #fffaf4;
        border: 1px solid #d8cabc;
        border-radius: 12px;
        box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(54, 39, 28, 0.08);
        padding: 1.5rem;
      }
      h1 {
        margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
        font-size: 1.75rem;
        line-height: 1.2;
      }
      p,
      li {
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      ul {
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
      }
      .callout {
        margin-top: 1rem;
        padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
        border-radius: 10px;
        background: #f7eee4;
        border: 1px solid #d8c4ad;
      }
        Step 8: Sources of Error and Suggestions for Improvement
          The original lesson file for this step was missing from the local course bundle, so this placeholder page
          keeps the module readable in local preview instead of dropping to a generic fallback card.
        When reviewing sources of error in a lab report, focus on the following questions:
          What factors could have affected the accuracy or consistency of the results?
          Which parts of the procedure may have introduced bias, measurement problems, or uncontrolled variables?
          What changes would improve the design if the experiment were repeated?
          How could the next version of the experiment produce clearer or more reliable data?
          Operator note
            Restore the original source file if it becomes available. Until then, this local placeholder prevents the
            Experimental Psychology course shell from breaking on this missing lesson resource.
